  "notes": [
    "Regular -AR verb, reflexive — the -ear ending keeps its \"e\" throughout and does not stem-change (like *pasear*, *desear*), even though it looks similar to e→ie verbs like *pensar*.",
    "Past participle is regular: **replanteado**.",
    "Imperativo afirmativo reflexive pronouns attach to the end with a written accent to preserve stress (replantéate, replantéese, replanteémonos, replantéense); imperativo negativo places them separately in front (no te replantees...).",
    "*Me replanteé mi carrera después del viaje.* (\"I reconsidered my career after the trip.\")",
    "*Deberías replantearte esa decisión.* (\"You should rethink that decision.\")",
    "Related: *plantear* (non-reflexive, \"to pose/raise\" a question or issue), *el planteamiento* (approach/premise, noun), *reconsiderar* (synonym, \"to reconsider\")."
  ],
